title: Anti-Fascist Day
subtitle: The party calls a day of action, and Prussia bans it.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 7
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('Prussia bans the Anti-Fascist Day', 2);
Q.sa_strength += 3;
Q.e23_afd_dead = 0;
!}

= Anti-Fascist Day

The Zentrale has called an Anti-Fascist Day for Sunday 29 July, with demonstrations in every city. The Prussian government bans all open-air meetings for that day, and other states follow. Then a telegram arrives from Moscow, signed by Radek: the Executive advises against risking a defeat in the streets. Zinoviev and Bukharin, people say, wanted the opposite.

- @march: March, ban or no ban.
- @indoor: Hold the meetings indoors in Prussia, and march where it is allowed.

@march
subtitle: Zinoviev will be pleased, Radek less so. Whether the police shoot is anyone's guess.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('radek', -6);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 6);
Q.e23_antifascist_day = 1;
Q.e23_afd_dead = Math.random() < 0.5 ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.e23_afd_dead) {
    RG.district('berlin', {repression: 10, militancy: 8, loyalty: 4});
    RG.news('Police fire on the Anti-Fascist Day in Berlin', 3);
} else {
    RG.district('berlin', {militancy: 5, members: 0.04});
    Q.worker_support += 4;
}
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

[? if e23_afd_dead = 1 : Forty thousand march in Berlin. The police charge on the Alexanderplatz and fire into the crowd. There are dead in Berlin, Frankfurt and Breslau. ?][? if e23_afd_dead = 0 : Forty thousand march in Berlin, and the police watch from their lorries and do nothing. The papers report that the communists held the city's streets for an afternoon. ?]

@indoor
subtitle: Radek's advice. In Saxony and Thuringia the hundreds march at the front.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('radek', 6);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -4);
RG.district('saxony', {militancy: 4, guards: 1});
RG.district('thuringia', {militancy: 4});
Q.e23_antifascist_day = 2;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 7;
!}

In Berlin the halls are full and the streets are quiet. In Saxony and Thuringia two hundred thousand march with the hundreds in front. Fischer calls it the day the Zentrale lost its nerve.
